   "reason": "The Dragon's attack set is queen rays plus knight squares, so detonating her is the largest blast in the game (attack set + ring 2 at T4+); the pair converts the game's shortest-lived summon into an immediate room clear plus a 2-3 turn stun. | The key on the king's diagonal is usually defended, which makes the bishop capture suicide; with the shield up she takes it anyway, absorbs the recapture, keeps the capture-stun and takes the king on the next move.",
